//? Title: Round-robin scheduling: actual arrivals, FIFO queues and quantum trade-offs
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Share one CPU among arriving processes with finite bursts, using bounded
execution quanta. Round-robin executes a ready process for at most one quantum
and requeues unfinished work behind intervening arrivals. Actual native dispatch
and queue histories replace report-local timeline helpers. The original four
simultaneous processes and quantum2 remain.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

For process i, turnaround is completion minus arrival and waiting is turnaround
minus burst. A positive quantum limits one dispatch to min(quantum,remaining)
busy ticks. During each real tick the native scheduler admits new arrivals in
input order; a preempted process joins behind them.
$$ T_i=C_i-A_i,\qquad W_i=T_i-B_i. $$
\alttext(Turnaround equals completion minus arrival; waiting subtracts actual required CPU burst.)
Small quanta can increase actual dispatches and preemptions; this simulation
assigns zero context-switch time, so no context-switch overhead is invented.
Zero-burst processes complete at their arrival. Idle gaps jump directly to the
next positive-work arrival and remain blank in the Gantt plot.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/round_robin_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto t = a::round_robin_trace({{7, 0, 3}, {91, 1, 1}}, 2);
    std::print("| selected input id | start | end | remaining before | remaining after | actual ready " "before | actual ready after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : t.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n",
                   s.process_index, s.start, s.end, s.remaining_before,
                   s.remaining_after, s.ready_before, s.ready_after);
    g::Diagram d(48, 1100);
    d.node("n0", {0, 0},
           std::format("Actual first dispatch input {}",
                       t.steps[0].process_index));
    d.node("n1", {5, 0},
           std::format("Actual first ready-after {}", t.steps[0].ready_after));
    d.node("n2", {10, 0},
           std::format("Actual completion of arriving job {}",
                       t.result.metrics[1].completion));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/round_robin_tiny.svg");
}
```
