> API and interpretation

Process ids are opaque and unique, not row indices. Arrival/burst and public
completion units are integral and checked. The native producer avoids the former
infinite loops on zero bursts/nonpositive quanta. Newly arrived jobs join before
a preempted job, with input-order arrival ties. Gantt merging can combine
contiguous dispatches of the same process, so dispatch counts come from actual
events rather than segment counts.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

